  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 214 AM EDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nSunday into at least Monday, most of the area should see northerly \nto northeasterly winds, bringing a \"cool\"down to more normal \ntemperatures for early September. By Tuesday the surface high \nbringing that cool down shifts into the NE US and we see a quick \nsoutherly return flow for midweek. Ridging builds in aloft as well, \nso temperatures will rebound just as quickly above normal. \n\nOur next cool front could move into the region Wednesday night into \nThursday time frame. Long Range Ensemble Forecast (LREF) has quite a \nbit of spread for temperatures and rain chances in that period and \ncontinuing to close out the work week.",
